 "signs": [
  {
   "x": 28,
   "y": 21,
   "text": "THE ENTRANCE STONE. Kerbstone K1, the great stone at the door, carved with triple spirals and lozenges. Nobody knows what the spirals meant. They're prehistoric art. They've been guessing for ten thousand years and still can't pin it down."
  },
  {
   "x": 32,
   "y": 21,
   "text": "THE ROOF BOX. Above the door a small slot lets the rising sun into the chamber for seventeen minutes around the winter solstice, 21 December. It's a calendar, a church and a lightbulb all in one, built five thousand years before anyone coined the term 'engineering'."
  },
  {
   "x": 11,
   "y": 26,
   "text": "BRU NA BOINNE VISITOR CENTRE. Tickets, a cafe and a replica of the passage. Newgrange tours go by shuttle bus over the river. The winter solstice places go by lottery, and some years it rains anyway."
  }
 ],
